note Exercism-style exercise "hello-world": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/hello-world
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note hello writes the greeting "Hello, World!" into o and returns its length in bytes.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/hello-world
om2
text hw "Hello, World!"
fn hello o edit uchar * to ulong
for i ulong len hw
put o i get hw i
end
ret len hw
end
